%description:

Tcp.lossDetectionMode:dupthresh -- two duplicate ACKs are not enough: only the timer repairs the loss.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "SACK loss detection: classic DupThresh (RFC 6675) or RACK time-based (RFC
8985)".

The classes: dupthresh (the value of LegacyTcp) and rack (the default, the value of LinuxTcp).
The code: with "rack", a segment is lost when a segment sent after it is SACKed and the time
RACK.rtt + the reordering window has passed (Rfc6675Recovery::rackDetectAndMarkLost(), with
the timer of the reordering window); with "dupthresh", at DupThresh duplicate ACKs, or when
IsLost() counts DupThresh SACKed segments above it (Rfc6675Recovery::receivedDuplicateAck()).
RACK needs SACK; without it, the connection uses DupThresh. This test separates "dupthresh" from "rack".

Host under test: host1, without the tail loss probe (precondition: the probe would repair the
loss in both classes), which sends three segments; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the first segment
once. host2 SACKs the other two: two duplicate ACKs, one less than DupThresh. Observation: level 1, no retransmission of the first segment in 0.5 s after the first
transmission; the timer retransmits it after about 1 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.lossDetectionMode
%# class: dupthresh
%# value: "dupthresh"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.lossDetectionMode
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpLossDetectionModeDupthresh")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the first data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the first data segment of host1")
             .within(2.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early retransmission of the first segment, by the timer")
              .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("retransmission of the first segment, by the timer")
             .within(1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpLossDetectionModeDupthresh compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.lossDetectionMode = "dupthresh"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 4344B
*.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpLossDetectionModeDupthresh: PASS
